@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+# Exact empty-LXC caller insertion map and dormant patch plan
+
+Pinned Incus a99413afd0c742da3bba10eb4f75d639f9dbbd32. This is source-inspected
+integration planning, not a complete callgraph proof or runnable patch. No
+upstream daemon hooks are changed. Native DB candidates remain unregistered.
+
+## New integration finding
+
+A guard immediately before `pool.CreateInstance` is TOO LATE for the entire
+empty-container path. `CreateInternal` calls native driver initialization and
+`lxcCreate` calls `devicesAdd` before returning. `CreateInternal` also invokes
+`os.RemoveAll(inst.LogPath())` and `os.RemoveAll(inst.RunPath())` when requested.
+Those effects require coverage independently of root storage creation. The
+single-effect DB candidate does not yet represent all supported-path attempts.
+
+## Transaction and caller chain (actual pinned symbols)
+
+1. `cmd/incusd/instances_post.go:instancesPost` authenticates through route
+   handling, decodes input and dispatches source-specific creation. Insert
+   bounded accepted envelope after verified principal/scope and BEFORE body
+   processing. Transport byte/time limits must be enforced here, not trusted
+   from the DB helper arguments. Binary backup and forwarding paths must be
+   rejected separately under the restricted profile.
+2. `cmd/incusd/instance.go:instanceCreateAsEmpty` invokes
+   `instance.CreateInternal(s,args,op,true,true)` and receives an operation lock
+   and cleanup hook. It then loads pool, calls `pool.CreateInstance`, registers
+   `inst.Delete(true)` cleanup and calls `inst.UpdateBackupFile`.
+3. `internal/server/instance/instance_utils.go:CreateInternal` resolves profiles,
+   takes `operationlock.Create(... ActionCreate ...)`, and opens a native
+   `s.DB.Cluster.Transaction`. Within it, the non-snapshot path calls
+   `cluster.CreateInstance`, creates devices/config, assigns profiles, reads
+   back the row and reconstructs arguments. Insert scope reservation and
+   immutable row binding in THIS same transaction, preserving all those native
+   mapper/config/device operations. The narrow candidate row insertion must
+   NOT replace the existing full native mapper path as-is.
+4. After transaction commit, CreateInternal registers name-based DB cleanup,
+   calls driver `Create`, registers its cleanup and removes old log/run paths.
+   Preserve retained guard history/reservation even if all ordinary row/config
+   rollback helpers succeed. A cleanup callback must not become an unjournaled
+   storage mutation just because it is a deferred error path.
+5. `internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go:lxcCreate` initializes and
+   validates expanded configuration/devices, loads the effective root pool,
+   assigns idmaps/volatile state, reinitializes, then calls `devicesAdd(d,false)`.
+   Effective profile/device configuration must be frozen or revision-checked
+   against the approved policy. A profile NAME alone is not a capability.
+6. `internal/server/storage/backend.go:CreateInstance` creates native volume DB
+   state, updates authorizer state, computes effective root volume overrides,
+   calls `b.driver.CreateVolume` with a rootfs filler, registers DeleteInstance
+   cleanup, creates instance symlink and schedules template application. Each
+   nested driver/filler and cleanup callback belongs to the accepted-work tree.
+7. UpdateBackupFile and outer deferred Delete/DB cleanup run after those steps.
+   Their success cannot produce physical release. A late error leaves retained
+   unresolved attempt(s), even when the visible native row was removed.
+
+## Minimal next insertion patch shape
+
+Do not wire the current DB candidate directly into step 2 and call it complete.
+First extend the native transaction API to support a bounded enumerated effect
+plan with parent/child attempts, exact immutable incarnation, policy digest and
+retained outcomes. The API must bind original controller lineage/reservation/
+dispatch identity and exact daemon/backend/project scope, not only request name.
+
+Then a dormant integration change should:
+
+- Add an internal opaque guarded-create context to the empty source dispatcher
+  and CreateInternal. No public JSON/config field may fabricate this capability.
+  Missing capability rejects guarded mode before the first possible effect.
+- Reserve canonical project/name/storage scope in the existing row transaction,
+  use the full native mapper and bind its newly inserted row/token before commit.
+  Unknown transaction commit does not invoke driver Create or repeat insertion.
+- Carry a native reservation through driver initialization, devicesAdd, log/run
+  preparation, backend CreateInstance, nested driver/filler, symlink/template
+  and backup stages. Commit distinct attempt before each effect boundary.
+  Record an observed return separately; do not infer terminal physical state.
+- Replace unguarded revert closures in the guarded branch with either typed,
+  journaled cleanup suboperations or intentional no-cleanup/retained leak.
+  Merely omitting outer inst.Delete does not suppress nested driver cleanup.
+- Deny all uncovered Start/Stop/reboot/autoRestart/native-ephemeral cleanup,
+  snapshots, rename/move, restore/rebuild, import/copy/image/migration and QEMU
+  at their native entrypoints for the guarded profile. Read-only admission at
+  the HTTP router cannot enforce internal paths or old in-flight handlers.
+- Leave the feature impossible to activate until the complete supported path
+  compiles and runs in a disposable native integration environment. Preserve
+  stock unguarded behavior only outside the unqualified experimental profile;
+  mixing stock writers into its managed scope is never permitted.
+
+**This is not yet a drop-in patch:** operation-lock ownership/handoff across
+nested callbacks and reentrant cleanup must be resolved before modifying live
+callers. There is no honest smaller active hook that covers the declared path.
+
+## Acceptance checks for that patch
+
+Use the actual `CreateInternal` mapper/config/device transaction (not the narrow
+candidate insertion) in native-package integration tests. Then build actual
+LXC/storage dependencies and fault the real daemon at every transition listed
+above. Assert no effect before a committed attempt, retained descendants after
+parent errors, no replay after restart/unknown commit, and no bypass through
+internal cleanup or native lifecycle. Audit denied paths via real calls, not
+just strings/AST checks. Pin actual effective profile/device/root pool policy.
+
+Actual cluster DB tests are currently feasible; full daemon compilation remains
+blocked on native dependencies and the reviewed disposable build recipe is not
+yet executed. cgroup facts and DB receipts do not establish whole-asset capacity,
+sole writer, anti-rollback lineage or job-intake fencing. No release API exists.
+
+## Dormant first native mapper bridge
+
+`guard_mapper_pending.go` now provides a non-exported, uncalled native DB helper
+that executes the actual generated `cluster.CreateInstance` mapper and binds
+its new row to retained history in the same transaction. It uses the existing
+native metadata fields rather than the earlier narrow raw INSERT. A savepoint
+rolls back the row/token if history insertion fails. Tests inject that failure
+and intentionally commit the outer transaction to verify no unbound row remains.
+The actual native prepared statement is used, with metadata preservation checked.
+
+The returned row can enter the existing one-shot database storage-attempt
+primitive. Neither helper invokes storage. Unsupported VM/snapshot/ephemeral/
+stateful rows are rejected. Source kind (empty versus image/import), native
+config/devices, effective policy, full CreateInternal transaction, daemon identity
+and original controller lineage are NOT represented by this mapper argument.
+Therefore this is not a safe public entrypoint or activation-ready capability.
+All missing checks remain hard integration prerequisites. No HTTP/native caller,
+feature flag or schema registration is added; unsupported daemon paths have NOT
+been globally fenced by adding this helper. Native locks and nested attempts
+remain as mapped above. Savepoint success is not transaction commit success;
+commit uncertainty must still forbid native I/O or replay.
+
+### Actual mapper-sequence composition test
+
+`guard_caller_pending_test.go` now composes the real native generated row,
+device and config mappers plus UpdateInstanceProfiles in a single SQLite
+transaction, following CreateInternal's non-snapshot database sequence. It
+uses actual prepared statements and native tables. An injected late config
+failure rolls back row/token/history/devices and retains the previously
+committed scope. Success preserves device/config/profile records and only
+then enters a separate retained storage-attempt transaction. No storage runs.
+This is mapper-sequence coverage, not execution of CreateInternal, device
+callbacks, native policy validation or daemon/cowsql commit faults.
+
+Unsupported-row regression cases now each have a fresh bound/reserved request
+and otherwise valid native object, so rejection cannot be attributed to a
+previously exhausted request or blank scope. They verify no row or history was
+inserted. No safety assertion or production check was relaxed.
