@@ -0,0 +1,218 @@
+# Proposed native guard integration: decision and patch contract
+
+Status: **proposal only**, pinned Incus `a99413afd0c742da3bba10eb4f75d639f9dbbd32`.
+No daemon hook, migration, storage driver or deployment is implemented here.
+The reviewed fixtures establish failure cases and source ordering, not native
+safety. This proposal advances from those cases to specific patch boundaries.
+
+## Decision
+
+Do not integrate automatic physical release next. Integrate a retained native
+attempt journal and fail-closed mutation capability first. A return from Incus,
+operation-list emptiness, row deletion or storage helper success will never
+release a charge. An incomplete native attempt blocks automatic replay and
+retains its reservation indefinitely. A later completion certificate needs a
+separate, driver-specific design and review.
+
+The initial candidate is a **single-node, non-clustered, LXC empty-container
+creation experiment**, not a runnable CI service. Empty containers do not by
+themselves provide a runner image/bootstrap; do not market this profile as a
+useful deployed GARM MVP. Image-backed creation is a subsequent traced path.
+
+## Durable native data contract
+
+Use the actual native database and its transaction API, not a second SQLite
+ledger. Table/column names below are proposed, not current upstream schema.
+
+- `guard_epoch`: deployment UUID, epoch, accepting/sealed. Deployment identity
+  must be externally bound against restoring an old DB; local epoch alone is
+  not anti-rollback.
+- `guard_requests`: UUID, authenticated principal, canonical scope, epoch,
+  requested verb, bounded body digest once decoded, immutable retained state.
+  Persist admission before body decoding, after authentication/authorization.
+  Reject reused UUID with differing scope, principal, verb or digest.
+- `guard_incarnations`: unpredictable immutable token, native instance ID,
+  project identity, request UUID. The current native row holds the same token;
+  history has no cascading delete. Never use configurable `volatile.uuid`.
+- `guard_attempts`: request UUID, incarnation token, monotonic suboperation
+  sequence, exact effect kind, epoch, `attempted` plus optional observed return.
+  Uniqueness is enforced in the database. Never update `attempted` into a state
+  meaning no physical effect merely because a callback returned an error.
+- `guard_reservations`: current identity/name reservation and unresolved parent
+  binding. Removal requires an independently qualified protocol, not row absence.
+
+Before allocating a native row, acquire a durable create-name/storage-scope
+reservation in the same native transaction. Reject ANY unresolved retained
+reservation for that native project/name/storage scope, even if its old row was
+cleaned up, its token differs, or the daemon restarted. ClaimRow must verify this
+exclusive pre-row reservation; a new token does not grant permission to reuse
+possibly occupied storage. Reservation keys must follow native canonical naming
+and all alias/rename rules, not caller-supplied display names.
+
+Pre-body acceptance must enforce per-principal and global bounded outstanding
+envelopes, body size and decode time. Disconnect, expiry or abandoned body marks
+the envelope abandoned but retains its identity and no-dispatch history; never
+discard it or automatically execute it later. Reclaiming envelope bookkeeping
+capacity requires proof that no native attempt was committed and all associated
+handlers are unable to dispatch; until that protocol exists, quotas fail closed.
+This is not release of a physical resource reservation.
+
+Accept, seal and row claim must serialize in native transactions. ClaimRow
+requires a matching current native row/token in the same transaction as row
+creation. Seal closes new acceptance and unclaimed row creation; it does NOT
+revoke an effect already durably attempted or stop a scheduled callback.
+
+## Required native primitive API
+
+These signatures are design pseudocode, not an exported implementation:
+
+```
+Accept(tx, authenticatedScope, epoch, requestID, verb) -> Request
+BindBody(tx, Request, digest) -> Request
+ReserveCreateScope(tx, Request, canonicalNativeScope) -> CreateReservation
+ClaimRow(tx, Request, CreateReservation, nativeID, immutableToken) -> Incarnation
+ReserveMutation(nativeOperationLock, Incarnation, verb) -> Reservation
+BeginAttempt(tx, Reservation, sequence, exactEffect) -> Attempt
+RecordObservedReturn(tx, Attempt, resultClass) // not physical completion
+Seal(tx, epoch) -> durable accepted/attempted frontier
+```
+
+`Reservation` and `Attempt` must be opaque native-owned handles. Guarded driver
+entrypoints must not accept an arbitrary boolean or caller-constructed token.
+Every actual side-effect method verifies its handle against the retained native
+record and the held identity reservation. Threading context only through HTTP
+handlers is insufficient: internal callbacks, reverts and backup entrypoints
+are independent paths. If native locks are reentrant or cannot span a callback,
+that path stays disabled until lock ordering and callback handoff are proven.
+
+Do not hold a SQL transaction over storage I/O. Commit BeginAttempt before I/O,
+while retaining the native identity/name reservation across the commit and call.
+On commit error/unknown ACK: make no new call; reopen/reconcile the unique record,
+but do not automatically execute an `attempted` record. After process restart,
+all such records remain unresolved, even if the effect may never have started.
+This intentionally trades liveness for avoiding duplicate effects.
+
+## Smallest production patch series to propose (not applied)
+
+1. **Native schema and transaction-only primitives.** Add native schema migration
+   and retained tables using the pinned native database mechanisms; add actual
+   DB tests for acceptance/claim/seal/rollback/reopen and immutable token checks.
+   Keep the feature non-activatable/default off. No HTTP success or physical
+   authority claim. Review generated mapper changes and history retention.
+2. **One guarded storage path plus deny coverage.** Trace empty LXC creation from
+   authenticated `instancesPost` through `CreateInternal` and `createAsEmpty`.
+   Persist attempt before `pool.CreateInstance`; preserve unresolved reservation
+   through backup-file creation, revert callbacks and row cleanup. Thread typed
+   capability to all participating methods. In the restrictive experiment,
+   deny image/copy/migration/backup/snapshot/restore/rebuild/rename/move and VM
+   paths before their first effect, at native entrypoints as well as routes.
+   Deny start/restart/autostart, hotplug and internal ephemeral deletion until
+   explicitly guarded. Unsupported cleanups may leak a resource intentionally;
+   they must not silently bypass the journal in the name of error recovery.
+3. **Disposable real-daemon qualification.** Build/link the exact fork with actual
+   native dependencies, run isolated native DB and LXC/storage fault tests,
+   and review the complete reachable mutation graph. Only then consider an
+   explicit experimental activation mode on a fresh dedicated instance.
+
+Patch 1 is the immediate implementation-sized step. Patches 2 and 3 are required
+before even the restricted profile is enforceable. Partial denial at the API
+router must never be described as completing patch 2. Until the native build
+recipe succeeds, neither compilation nor integration feasibility is verified.
+
+## Failure obligations derived from reviewed seams
+
+| Seam | Required insertion and unresolved obligation |
+| --- | --- |
+| Empty creation | Row commit precedes storage; journal before storage; retain history if revert removes row. |
+| Rebuild | First destructive DeleteInstance needs reservation and attempt, not a later config transaction. Delete/create are separate sequenced effects; interruption cannot restart the whole prefix. Initially denied. |
+| Backup import | Storage can begin before instance row. Requires separate import identity and scope reservation, not ClaimRow on a nonexistent instance; failed cleanup remains unresolved. Initially denied. |
+| Internal onStop | Reboot/autoRestart calls Start; otherwise native ephemeral cleanup calls internal delete(true). API admission does not see these. Deny unsupported callback transitions at their actual native entrypoints, not by assuming GitHub JIT implies native ephemeral. |
+| Delete | Existing native lock plus immutable current incarnation recheck BEFORE devices/storage. Name-targeted database deletion afterwards is not protection. Initially denied. |
+| Return/operation record | Observed success/error is only a receipt; expiry and authorization-filtered lists cannot drain the frontier. |
+
+## Qualification tests that move beyond the fixtures
+
+- Actual native DB migration forward/reopen and concurrent accept/seal/claim;
+  durable unknown-commit fault, history surviving native-row deletion. Reject
+  creation with a new token into an unresolved old project/name/storage scope
+  after row cleanup and database reopen. Exercise alias/canonical-name collisions.
+- Real dispatcher attempts before body completion; no admitted untracked handler;
+  authenticated local socket and cluster refusal paths included. Bound pending
+  body envelopes; exercise disconnect/timeout before and during decode, retain
+  abandoned identity, and deny delayed execution/replay after abandonment.
+- Fork process killed at committed attempt/before call, during storage, and after
+  storage/before outcome receipt. Restart must retain reservation and never replay.
+- Actual storage driver leaves a resource after injected return/cleanup failure;
+  row cleanup cannot release reservation. Test each supported storage backend.
+- Internal callback invoked after API response/seal; reject unsupported restart
+  and delete before effects. Test name reuse, rename and restoration attempts
+  against reserved incarnation, without relying on inventory visibility.
+- Negative activation tests: pre-existing unknown resources/requests, unsupported
+  type/path, alternate writer, old database lineage, incomplete host ownership.
+
+## External prerequisites still required
+
+An enforceable native resource parent covering the entire intended physical
+asset, sole writer/whole-asset ownership, trusted root/admin boundary, complete
+local/internal ingress coverage and externally anchored database lineage are
+not provided by these tables or fixtures. Container cgroup facts do not cover
+QEMU/VM memory or every out-of-band writer. A hostile host administrator is
+outside the enforceable boundary; such a host cannot be qualified by this API.
+
+Keep controller provisioning disabled unless its independently required
+capacity/scope/writer/lineage gates are actually satisfied. Do not increase
+budget or reset/recreate a ledger to work around retained unknowns. This series
+contains no manual or automatic release mechanism and no live rollout approval.
+
+## Offline first native-package candidate
+
+`internal/server/db/cluster/guard_pending.go` is now an unregistered migration
+and unexported transaction primitive candidate in the actual pinned native DB
+package. There are no daemon callers, activation setting, `updates` registration
+or generated fresh-schema changes. Migration initializes a sealed epoch. Tests
+explicitly unseal their disposable database, never a running installation.
+
+Tests append the candidate via native `Schema().Add`/`ExerciseUpdate`, applying
+real upstream migrations and using real native instances/projects/pool tables.
+They check retained scope after actual instance row deletion, SQLite snapshot
+file reopen, rollback, sealed admission, abandoned/expired body binding refusal,
+principal mismatch, per-principal/global retained-envelope caps and oversize
+body refusal. Race instrumentation does not by itself establish concurrent
+transaction ordering, and file reopen is not a killed-daemon crash test.
+
+Implemented scope is acceptance/body binding/abandonment, pre-row create scope
+reservation and sealing ONLY. ClaimRow/current immutable native token, native
+attempt journal, canonical alias resolution, native locks, authenticated route
+integration and body-stream limits remain unimplemented. Caller-supplied byte
+count/principal are inputs, not verified transport facts. Reservation checks
+existing native DB rows/volumes but cannot detect unrecorded physical storage;
+fresh enrollment and complete writer coverage remain prerequisites. No output
+from these methods is authority to dispatch physical work. The unregistered
+migration intentionally cannot be activated by restarting an ordinary daemon.
+
+### Offline row/attempt follow-on
+
+The separate follow-on adds an immutable nullable token on the real `instances`
+table within the still-unregistered migration. `guardCreateRow` inserts a narrow
+empty/non-ephemeral container row itself and binds retained history in the same
+caller transaction; it cannot adopt an existing row. It is NOT the full native
+CreateInternal mapper/config/device path. The caller must roll back on error,
+as with native transaction helpers. Existing unguarded rows remain nullable and
+are not enrolled or treated as qualified.
+
+`guardBeginStorage` records one `create_storage` attempt per request, after
+checking retained reservation/history/current row identity and the live epoch.
+It permits no generic delete, restore, image or lifecycle effect. Successful
+commit is necessary but insufficient for I/O: native identity locking, full
+scope policy and actual effect-site wiring remain missing. Unknown commit must
+not trigger I/O/retry. A stored attempt after restart is NOT a work queue.
+`guardRecordStorageReturn` records one success/error receipt, including after
+seal or row cleanup, and never removes scope/history or releases a charge.
+
+Actual native-schema tests now include row/history transaction rollback,
+non-adoption, immutable token enforcement, changed native name refusal, attempt
+retention through row removal and SQLite file reopen, post-seal observed return,
+no repeated attempt/receipt and retained scope after either return. No storage
+callback is invoked. Unknown ACK is modeled by omitting the return receipt,
+not by a killed daemon or faulted cowsql commit. Migration is still unregistered
+and no production daemon can activate this through configuration.
