+++ b/qualification/native-reservation-propagation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Typed reservation propagation: next dormant integration boundary
+
+Design only, pinned Incus a99413afd0c742da3bba10eb4f75d639f9dbbd32. No caller,
+capability issuer, native hook or activation setting is installed by this file.
+This document narrows the earlier insertion map; it does not claim that a type
+alone enforces native storage or protects against an untrusted host root.
+
+## Issuance and ownership
+
+Introduce one internal native guard service owned by daemon state. It owns the
+native DB handle and installed deployment identity, not an arbitrary caller
+supplied `Journal` interface. Its admission route must verify the original
+controller lineage/reservation/dispatch identity, daemon/backend/project,
+canonical resource scope and effective policy digest. A plain request UUID or
+label cannot substitute for that binding.
+
+The service returns a pointer to an opaque `CreateReservation` with private
+fields; only the issuer package constructs it. The same pointer carries native
+operation-lock ownership (or a checked lock lease) across callers. Avoid serializing
+this live capability into user config, operation metadata or volatile.uuid. A
+restarted process reloads unresolved history for reporting, NOT runnable handles.
+
+`BeginEffect` returns a process-local, one-use `EffectPermit` only after its
+native transaction has definitely committed. An ambiguous commit returns no
+permit; reopening an existing attempt must never reconstruct one. Caller cannot
+choose an arbitrary effect kind or sequence: these come from an issuer-owned,
+versioned allowlist plan bound to the effective policy. Delivery/consumption of
+a permit still needs a real native reservation and effect-site check; a copied
+pointer or Go type is not sufficient proof.
+
+## Explicit proposed call propagation
+
+Signatures below describe a future guarded branch, not current compiled APIs:
+
+```
+instanceCreateAsEmptyGuarded(..., create *nativeguard.CreateReservation)
+  -> CreateInternalGuarded(..., create)
+     -> existing native mapper/config/device transaction + identity binding
+     -> guarded driver Create(..., create)
+        -> lxcCreate(..., create)
+           -> devicesAddGuarded(..., create)
+              -> deviceAddGuarded(device, create.BeginEffect(devicePlanEntry))
+  -> pool.CreateInstanceGuarded(..., create)
+     -> guarded CreateVolume + rootfs filler + symlink/template child attempts
+  -> UpdateBackupFileGuarded(..., create)
+```
+
+Missing context fails before effects in the guarded branch. Do not silently
+fall back to the unguarded method when a guard error occurs. Stock paths outside
+the candidate scope are not transformed into qualified writers by preserving
+their behavior. A dedicated guarded daemon must reject those mutation paths.
+
+The database mapper bridge currently binds a row and one attempt only. Before
+this call chain can compile honestly, its native transaction contract needs
+policy/source/lineage binding, a bounded child-effect plan and checked native
+lock handoff. It is not safe to promote the existing one-shot create_storage
+helper as a grant for all initialization effects.
+
+## Pre-storage device effects and cleanup
+
+Actual pinned `common.devicesAdd` loads each effective device and calls
+`deviceAdd` -> `dev.Add()`. It registers `deviceRemove` -> `dev.Remove()` as a
+revert. Validation errors may call `deviceVolatileReset`; conflict errors can
+skip adding a device. Therefore the plan must bind the exact expanded ordered
+device set and distinguish attempted, deliberately skipped, error and cleanup.
+Never treat returning a revert hook as proof cleanup ran or succeeded.
+
+A useful minimization for the INITIAL NON-RUNNING EXPERIMENT is an exact root
+ disk-only policy, no NIC/other devices. The pinned disk type embeds
+`deviceCommon` and has no Add override; deviceCommon.Add returns nil. This
+reduces the immediate Add effect surface, but is NOT a proof that device loading,
+validation, idmap allocation or all surrounding driver initialization is pure.
+Those calls still require trace/qualification. No networked CI service is
+claimed by this intentionally incomplete profile.
+
+Guarded cleanup must consume its own predeclared cleanup permit before Remove.
+If not yet supported, retain the original reservation and report leaked/unknown;
+do not invoke an unguarded cleanup as an emergency escape. Cleanup loops and
+nested storage-driver reverts need the same rule, not only the outer hook.
+
+## Log/run path handling
+
+Current empty-create calls CreateInternal with clearLogDir=true, causing two
+post-row `os.RemoveAll` calls. The narrow guarded branch should set clearLogDir
+FALSE and reject preexisting path conflicts rather than delete them. This is a
+new restricted branch behavior, not a reinterpretation of today's tests.
+
+A pathname existence check is not identity-safe deletion authorization. If log
+cleanup is later required, it needs an anchored directory capability, retained
+path/incarnation binding, symlink/mount/race controls and a separate typed effect
+permit. Never reuse the storage-create permit for RemoveAll. Disabling cleanup
+also requires proving later create/log code cannot truncate or replace those
+preexisting paths; the preflight check alone is not that proof.
+
+## Integration test acceptance, not another stand-alone boolean model
+
+1. Build the real guarded call chain against pinned native drivers and state.
+2. Exercise real effective root-only policy and reject altered profiles/device
+   order/source kind before creation or device callbacks.
+3. Inject native DB commit uncertainty: no EffectPermit, no device/storage call.
+4. Run real caller failure/revert paths: every reached cleanup is denied or has
+   a distinct committed child attempt; no raw fallback.
+5. Prove native locks remain held/revalidated across initialization and callback
+   boundaries; test delayed calls after seal and restart without issuing permits.
+6. Show log/run conflicts cannot be deleted/truncated through any supported path.
+
+Daemon native dependencies remain unbuilt here. These gates cannot be replaced
+by the passing SQLite/native-mapper tests. No physical release is proposed.
