+# Disposable native compile recipe (prepared, not executed)
+
+This recipe attempts a pinned-source Incus daemon **compile only** and runs the
+nonprivileged qualification fixtures. It does not run Incus, mount a host socket,
+request devices/privileged mode, change live hosts, or grant release authority.
+The current workspace has neither Docker nor Podman. Therefore this recipe has
+NOT built an image or verified package availability; do not report it passing.
+
+Use a disposable trusted build worker. Supply a verified official Debian 13 slim
+image by immutable manifest digest, not a moving tag:
+
+```
+qualification/nativebuild/run.sh docker.io/library/debian@sha256:<verified-64-hex-digest>
+```
+
+The digest must identify Debian **13**. The script validates official image name
+and digest syntax; it cannot derive distro version from a hash. The Dockerfile
+uses that official image's signed distro apt sources, no third-party package
+repository/install script. Before execution review the resolved image and apt
+sources. Go uses the pinned source go.mod/go.sum; downloaded dependency checksums
+are verified by Go. No user credentials are supplied.
+
+Exact resolved package versions are generated in `/out/native-package-versions.tsv`,
+with Go version/environment in `/out`. These values are **unknown until a real
+build succeeds**, not guessed. The base digest and source commit must accompany
+any build evidence. Apt repositories may evolve; exact package manifest captures
+that build but alone does not make future builds reproducible. A subsequent
+qualified workflow should pin a verified official snapshot/versions.
+
+The compile artifact `/out/incusd-compile-only.test` must NOT be executed. Fixture
+success uses fake storage/row objects and cannot establish native driver semantics,
+complete mutation coverage, cowsql transaction behavior, or safe capacity release.
+Do not run this on a production runner with secrets or combine it with live Incus.
+There is intentionally no auto-triggered CI workflow or automatic publishing here.
